messages.content:
{
  "understanding": "You now have 3 bars on 4G, which is good, but the speed test still says No Connection. That means your phone is registered to the network, but the actual data session isn’t establishing. The most common causes at this point are APN selection not applied, a glitch with the data toggle/roaming toggle, or a SIM registration hiccup while roaming.",
  "what_we_will_try_next_and_why": [
    "Rebuild the data session by toggling Data and Roaming: this forces the phone to request a fresh data connection on the roaming network.",
    "Verify the APN list and which APN is selected: after a reset, sometimes no APN is selected or the wrong one is active, which blocks data even when 4G shows.",
    "Reseat the SIM: this refreshes network registration while roaming.",
    "Then allow 5G again (if available) for best possible speed."
  ],
  "steps_on_your_phone": [
    {
      "step": "Rebuild the data session",
      "instructions": [
        "Go to Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network.",
        "Turn Mobile data OFF, wait 10 seconds, then turn it ON.",
        "Turn Data roaming OFF, wait 10 seconds, then turn it ON.",
        "Wait 30–60 seconds and watch that it stays on 4G with 2–4 bars."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Verify APN selection",
      "instructions": [
        "Still in Mobile network, tap Access Point Names (APN).",
        "Check if there is at least one APN listed and which one has the filled radio dot (selected).",
        "If NONE is selected, tap the default APN to select it.",
        "If the list is EMPTY, tap the menu (⋮) and choose Reset to default again, then check that an APN appears and is selected.",
        "If there are multiple APNs and you’re not sure which to use, please tell me the APN names you see so I can advise which to select."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Test quickly",
      "instructions": [
        "Open your browser and try loading a website.",
        "If it loads, also try fast.com and note the speed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "If still no data: reseat the SIM",
      "instructions": [
        "Power the phone OFF.",
        "Remove the SIM tray, take the SIM out, and reinsert it firmly.",
        "Put the tray back and power the phone ON.",
        "Confirm: Mobile data ON, Data roaming ON.",
        "Keep Preferred network type on 4G only for the moment and wait 30–60 seconds.",
        "Try a website and then fast.com again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Allow 5G again for best speed (after it starts working)",
      "instructions": [
        "Change Preferred network type back to 5G/4G (LTE) preferred.",
        "Test fast.com again for the best available speed."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "please_reply_with": [
    "What you saw in the APN list (names and which one is selected).",
    "Whether toggling Mobile data and Data roaming helped.",
    "Whether you reseated the SIM and what changed after.",
    "The fast.com speed once it connects."
  ],
  "next_if_unresolved": "If data still won’t pass on 4G after these steps, I can transfer you to a human roaming specialist to check the specific partner network at your location and refresh your roaming profile from our side."
}

