messages.content:
{
  "message": "2G is too slow for MMS. Let’s switch your phone to prefer 4G/5G, refresh the connection, and test again.",
  "thought_process": "Your line is active and has data remaining, so the bottleneck is the phone connecting on 2G. MMS typically requires at least 3G and works best on 4G/5G. We’ll change the preferred network type, refresh radios, and retest. If it still sticks to 2G (coverage), we’ll try an APN reset and other settings.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Set Preferred Network to 4G/5G",
      "why": "For MMS to work reliably, your phone should connect to 4G/5G instead of 2G.",
      "instructions": [
        "On Android: Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network (or SIMs).",
        "Tap Preferred network type (or Network mode).",
        "Select 5G/4G (LTE) preferred or 4G/5G auto. If you see a ‘Allow 2G’ toggle, turn it OFF."
      ],
      "device_action_hint": "Use set_network_mode_preference to 4g_5g_preferred."
    },
    {
      "title": "Refresh the connection",
      "why": "Forces the phone to re-register on a faster network after the change.",
      "instructions": [
        "Turn Airplane mode ON for ~15 seconds, then turn it OFF.",
        "Ensure Mobile data is ON and Wi‑Fi stays OFF for this test."
      ],
      "device_action_hint": "toggle_airplane_mode, toggle_data"
    },
    {
      "title": "Test",
      "instructions": [
        "Check the status bar: does it now show 4G/LTE/5G instead of 2G?",
        "Open a web page on mobile data.",
        "Try sending an MMS (e.g., a photo) to your own number."
      ],
      "please_report_back": [
        "What network type do you see now (4G/LTE/5G or still 2G)?",
        "Could you load a web page?",
        "Did the MMS send?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "If it still shows 2G or MMS won’t send",
      "instructions": [
        "Move closer to a window or step outside for better signal, wait ~30–60 seconds, and recheck the network type.",
        "Turn OFF Data Saver: Settings > Network & Internet > Data Saver (set to Off).",
        "If you use a VPN, disconnect it temporarily.",
        "Retry the Test step."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "If it still fails: Reset APN and reboot",
      "why": "Ensures correct mobile data/MMSC settings for MMS.",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet > Mobile network > Access Point Names.",
        "Tap the menu and choose Reset to default.",
        "Restart your phone.",
        "With Wi‑Fi OFF and Mobile data ON, try the web page and send an MMS again."
      ],
      "device_action_hint": "reset_apn_settings, reboot_device"
    },
    {
      "title": "Optional: Toggle Wi‑Fi Calling OFF for MMS test",
      "why": "On some setups, Wi‑Fi Calling can interfere with MMS.",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet > Wi‑Fi Calling > turn OFF.",
        "Retest MMS on mobile data."
      ],
      "note": "You can re-enable Wi‑Fi Calling after testing."
    }
  ],
  "question": "Please try Steps 1–3 now and tell me: the network type you see (4G/LTE/5G or 2G), whether a web page loads, and if the MMS sends. If not improved, proceed with Step 4 and let me know the results. We’ll keep going until it’s fixed."
}

