messages.content:
{
  "message": "Great job getting your phone onto 5G with strong signal. Since mobile data is fast but MMS still fails, the most common remaining causes are Wi‑Fi Calling interference, Data Saver/VPN restrictions, APN/MMSC configuration, or app permissions. Let’s go step by step.",
  "thought_process": "MMS needs working mobile data (you have it), plus correct APN/MMSC and app permissions. Wi‑Fi Calling and Data Saver/VPN can also block MMS. We’ll disable potential blockers, then verify/reset APN (which sets the MMSC), and finally confirm the Messages app has required permissions.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Turn OFF Wi‑Fi Calling for this test",
      "why": "On some setups, Wi‑Fi Calling can interfere with MMS delivery.",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Wi‑Fi Calling.",
        "Turn Wi‑Fi Calling OFF.",
        "Ensure Wi‑Fi is OFF and Mobile data is ON.",
        "Try sending an MMS again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Ensure no data restrictions",
      "why": "Data Saver and VPN can block/slow MMS traffic.",
      "instructions": [
        "Data Saver: Settings > Network & Internet > Data Saver > set to Off.",
        "VPN: Settings > Network & Internet > VPN > disconnect any active VPN.",
        "Retest sending an MMS with Wi‑Fi OFF and Mobile data ON."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check/Reset APN (MMSC) and reboot",
      "why": "MMS depends on the MMSC URL in your APN. A wrong/missing MMSC commonly breaks MMS.",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet > Mobile network > Access Point Names.",
        "Open the active APN and look for an MMSC field. If it’s missing or you’re unsure:",
        "Tap the menu and choose ‘Reset to default’.",
        "Restart your phone to apply changes.",
        "After reboot: keep Wi‑Fi OFF, ensure Mobile data ON, confirm you see 4G/5G, then try sending an MMS again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Confirm Messages app permissions",
      "why": "The app must have SMS and storage/media permissions to send/attach photos.",
      "instructions": [
        "Settings > Apps > Messages (your default messaging app) > Permissions.",
        "Allow: SMS (or Messages) and Storage/Photos & media.",
        "Reopen the Messages app and try sending an MMS again."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "please_report_back": [
    "Was Wi‑Fi Calling ON, and did turning it OFF help?",
    "Is Data Saver OFF and VPN disconnected?",
    "Did you reset APN and reboot? After that, did MMS send?",
    "Were SMS and Storage/Photos & media permissions allowed for Messages?"
  ],
  "next_if_still_failing": "If MMS still won’t send after these steps, tell me exactly where it failed and any error you now see. We can continue with targeted checks, and if it persists after all troubleshooting, I’ll escalate you to a human agent."
}

