messages.content:
{
  "acknowledgement": "Great progress, John. Airplane Mode is off and the SIM is active now. The remaining blocker is that your phone is currently on 2G, which is generally not suitable for MMS. We’ll switch your network mode to prefer 4G/5G, then verify APN/MMSC, and test again.",
  "thought_process": "MMS needs any working mobile data plus a correct MMSC server setting. Being on 2G prevents MMS from sending. So first we’ll change the network mode to allow 4G/5G. If MMS still fails, the next most common cause is APN/MMSC configuration. We’ll then rule out Data Saver/VPN or Wi‑Fi Calling interactions.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Switch network mode to allow 4G/5G",
      "why": "2G is not adequate for MMS. Preferring 4G/5G restores data capability for picture messages.",
      "instructions": [
        "Run: check_network_mode_preference.",
        "If it shows 2G or 3G, change it to 4g_5g_preferred using: set_network_mode_preference(mode=\"4g_5g_preferred\").",
        "After changing the mode, refresh the data connection: toggle_data OFF, wait 5 seconds, then toggle_data ON.",
        "Run: check_network_status and share the new network type (aiming for 4G/5G or at least 3G) and signal strength."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Try sending an MMS again (with Wi‑Fi OFF)",
      "why": "Confirms whether the network mode change resolved it.",
      "instructions": [
        "Keep Wi‑Fi OFF for this test.",
        "Open your messaging app and send a picture to any contact.",
        "If it still fails, continue to the next step."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Verify APN/MMSC settings",
      "why": "A missing/incorrect MMSC in the APN commonly causes MMS to hang at “Sending…”.",
      "instructions": [
        "Run: check_apn_settings and note whether an MMSC URL is shown.",
        "If MMSC is missing or you’re unsure, reset to defaults: reset_apn_settings.",
        "After resetting APN, reboot to apply: reboot_device.",
        "When the phone is back on, run: check_network_status to confirm you’re on 4G/5G (or 3G), then try sending an MMS again (Wi‑Fi still OFF for the test)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rule out Data Saver or VPN interference",
      "why": "These can block or slow MMS.",
      "instructions": [
        "Run: check_data_restriction_status. If Data Saver is ON, turn it OFF: toggle_data_saver_mode.",
        "Run: check_vpn_status. If a VPN is connected, disconnect it: disconnect_vpn.",
        "Retry sending an MMS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check Wi‑Fi Calling",
      "why": "Certain configurations can interfere with MMS.",
      "instructions": [
        "Run: check_wifi_calling_status.",
        "If ON, turn it OFF: toggle_wifi_calling.",
        "Retry sending an MMS (keep Wi‑Fi OFF during the test)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Optional: Quick app capability check",
      "why": "Confirms the messaging app is allowed to send MMS.",
      "instructions": [
        "Run: can_send_mms and share the result.",
        "If it reports missing permissions, run: check_app_permissions(app_name=\"messaging\"). If storage or sms is not granted, grant them: grant_app_permission(app_name=\"messaging\", permission=\"storage\") and grant_app_permission(app_name=\"messaging\", permission=\"sms\").",
        "Test MMS again."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "what_to_send_me": [
    "From Step 1: Your network mode before/after, and the new check_network_status (network type and signal strength).",
    "From Step 3: Whether MMSC was present; confirm if you reset APN and rebooted.",
    "Whether Data Saver or a VPN was active and if turning them off helped.",
    "Wi‑Fi Calling status and whether turning it off helped.",
    "Whether MMS succeeded after each step."
  ],
  "note": "Please start with Step 1 to get off 2G, then test. If it still fails, proceed to Step 3. Share the results and I’ll adjust the next steps as needed."
}

