messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for the detailed update. Since mobile data works and MMS fails only when Wi‑Fi Calling is ON, this points to how MMS is routed when Wi‑Fi Calling is active. Let’s try a few targeted Android checks to get both working together.",
  "plan": [
    {
      "step": "Turn Wi‑Fi ON and connect to your usual Wi‑Fi network (keep Wi‑Fi Calling ON and Mobile Data ON).",
      "why": "On some Android devices, MMS over Wi‑Fi Calling only works when you’re actually connected to Wi‑Fi.",
      "do_this": [
        "Enable Wi‑Fi and connect to your home network.",
        "Send a test picture message."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Make sure Data Saver is OFF.",
      "why": "Data Saver can block background data the messaging app needs for MMS.",
      "android_path": "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Data Saver > OFF",
      "then": "Try sending an MMS again."
    },
    {
      "step": "Disconnect any VPN (if you use one).",
      "why": "A VPN tunnel can interfere with MMS while Wi‑Fi Calling is active.",
      "android_path": "Settings > Network & Internet > VPN (or your VPN app) > Disconnect",
      "then": "Try sending an MMS again."
    },
    {
      "step": "Confirm messaging app permissions.",
      "why": "The app must have Storage and SMS permissions to send picture messages.",
      "android_path": "Settings > Apps > [Your messaging app] > Permissions > Allow Storage and SMS",
      "then": "Try sending an MMS again."
    },
    {
      "step": "Verify preferred network mode is 4G/5G.",
      "why": "Ensures the phone isn’t falling back to a mode that can complicate MMS with Wi‑Fi Calling.",
      "android_path": "Settings > Network & Internet > Mobile network > Preferred network type > 4G/5G (or 5G/LTE/Auto)",
      "then": "Try sending an MMS again."
    },
    {
      "step": "Refresh Wi‑Fi Calling registration.",
      "why": "A quick off/on can re-register services cleanly after the APN reset.",
      "do_this": [
        "Turn Wi‑Fi Calling OFF, wait 10 seconds, then turn it ON again.",
        "Keep Mobile Data ON and (preferably) stay connected to Wi‑Fi.",
        "Try sending an MMS again."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "ask": "Please work through the steps in order and tell me which one (if any) makes MMS work with Wi‑Fi Calling ON. Also, which messaging app are you using (e.g., Google Messages, Samsung Messages)?",
  "if_persists": "If MMS still fails only when Wi‑Fi Calling is ON after these steps, I can escalate to a human specialist to review Wi‑Fi Calling/MMS provisioning on the network side, or you can use the immediate workaround of turning Wi‑Fi Calling OFF only when sending MMS. Let me know which you prefer."
}

