messages.content:
{
  "summary": "Because your phone says “No SIM card detected,” we must resolve that first. If the phone can’t see a SIM (physical or eSIM), it cannot register on any network—so changing network mode or enabling roaming won’t help yet.",
  "how_to_check_if_physical_sim_or_esim": [
    {
      "method": "Look for a SIM tray on the phone",
      "steps": [
        "Inspect the phone’s edges. A physical SIM tray usually has a small pinhole next to a thin outline. If you see this, you have a physical SIM slot.",
        "If there’s no tray (and the back doesn’t open), your phone may be eSIM‑only or using eSIM."
      ]
    },
    {
      "method": "Check in Settings",
      "steps": [
        "Open Settings > Network & Internet > SIMs (or Mobile Network). On some phones it’s Settings > Connections > SIM manager.",
        "On that screen, note exactly what you see:",
        "- An entry for “SIM 1” or “Physical SIM” (with your number/carrier) means a physical SIM is expected.",
        "- A section labeled “eSIM,” a toggle for your carrier line, or a button “Add eSIM” indicates eSIM capability.",
        "- If you only see “Add eSIM” and no physical SIM listed, you’re likely using (or should use) eSIM."
      ]
    },
    {
      "method": "About phone > IMEI/EID",
      "steps": [
        "Go to Settings > About phone > IMEI (or Status).",
        "If you see an EID number, the device supports eSIM. If you see entries like “IMEI (slot 1)” only, that suggests a physical SIM slot is present.",
        "This doesn’t confirm which one is active, but helps identify capability."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "what_to_do_next_based_on_what_you_find": {
    "if_physical_sim_present": [
      "Power the phone OFF.",
      "Eject the SIM tray with a SIM tool or paperclip, remove the SIM.",
      "Gently wipe the gold contacts with a soft, dry cloth. Check for dust or damage.",
      "Reinsert the SIM in the correct orientation and fully seat the tray.",
      "Power ON and wait 1–2 minutes.",
      "Then check: do you now see signal bars and does SIM status change from “No SIM card detected”?"
    ],
    "if_using_esim_or_no_tray_found": [
      "Restart the phone.",
      "Go to Settings > Network & Internet > SIMs (or Mobile Network).",
      "If your carrier line appears under eSIM, make sure its toggle is ON.",
      "If you see only “Add eSIM” (no carrier line listed), tell me exactly what options you see. We may need to re‑add your eSIM profile."
    ]
  },
  "after_sim_is_detected_configure_roaming": [
    "Set Preferred network type to 4G/5G (not 2G only).",
    "Turn Data Roaming ON.",
    "Turn Wi‑Fi OFF temporarily and test a webpage, then try an MMS."
  ],
  "please_reply_with": [
    "Do you see a physical SIM tray on the phone?",
    "In Settings > SIMs (or SIM manager), what exact entries and buttons do you see (e.g., SIM 1, eSIM toggle, Add eSIM)?",
    "Under About phone > IMEI/Status, do you see an EID listed?",
    "After reseating (if physical) or enabling (if eSIM), does the status change from “No SIM card detected” and do any signal bars appear?"
  ],
  "why_these_steps": "If the device can’t detect a SIM/eSIM profile, it cannot attach to any network. Once the SIM is recognized, we’ll enable roaming and set 4G/5G so you can register on a French network and send MMS."
}

