messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for the update. “No Service” means the phone isn’t registering on any cellular network yet, so MMS can’t work. The two biggest blockers I see from what you shared are: (1) Network mode was set to 2G only, which can prevent connection, and (2) Data roaming was OFF while you’re abroad. We’ll fix registration first, then test MMS.",
  "do_this_in_order": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "action": "Confirm Airplane Mode is OFF (or toggle it ON for 5 seconds, then OFF).",
      "why": "This resets the radios and often clears a stuck ‘No Service’ state."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "action": "Change Preferred Network Type to 4G/5G (Auto).",
      "path_example_android": "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Preferred network type > 5G/4G/3G/2G (Auto) or LTE/5G",
      "why": "2G-only can block registration where modern networks require 4G/5G."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "action": "Turn Data Roaming ON.",
      "path_example_android": "Settings > Network & Internet > Mobile network > Data roaming ON",
      "why": "You’re abroad; roaming must be allowed for mobile data (required for MMS)."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "action": "Turn Wi‑Fi Calling OFF temporarily.",
      "path_example_android": "Settings > Network & Internet > Mobile network > Wi‑Fi Calling OFF",
      "why": "Removes a variable while we re-register to the roaming network."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "action": "Force a network re-registration.",
      "options": [
        "Preferred: Settings > Mobile network > Network operators > set to Automatic.",
        "If already Automatic: choose Search networks, then manually pick any available network. If it fails, try another. After connecting, you can return to Automatic."
      ],
      "why": "Prompts the phone to attach to a compatible roaming partner."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "action": "If it still shows ‘No Service’, restart the phone.",
      "why": "A full reboot refreshes all radio and network stacks."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "action": "If still no service after reboot, check SIM status.",
      "path_example_android": "Settings > About phone > SIM status",
      "what_to_look_for": [
        "If it says Missing/Not detected: power off, remove and reinsert the SIM, power on, then re-check.",
        "If it says Locked (PIN/PUK): tell me what you see—we’ll handle that next."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "after_service_returns": [
    "With signal bars showing and 4G/5G/LTE indicated, keep Wi‑Fi OFF and mobile data ON.",
    "Try sending a new MMS (a small photo to your own number is fine)."
  ],
  "notes_on_your_account": {
    "line_status": "Active",
    "roaming_enabled_on_carrier_side": true,
    "data_refuel": "2 GB added successfully, so you now have data available for MMS."
  },
  "request": "Please go through steps 1–5 in order. After step 5, tell me what the status bar shows (signal bars and network type like 4G/5G/LTE) and whether it still says ‘No Service’. If it does, proceed to step 6 and 7 and let me know exactly what you see in SIM status."
}

